# Never banned by mqtt-area-ban: one IP or CIDR per line, '#' starts a comment.
# Copy to allow.txt (ignored by git) and add your own networks. tools/deploy.sh installs
# it as /etc/mqtt-area-ban/allow.txt; without allow.txt it keeps the file already on the
# server, or installs this example on a first deploy.
# Loopback and the host's own addresses are always allowed and don't need a line.

# 198.51.100.0/24   # e.g. your home network
# 2001:db8::/48     # IPv6 works too
